    doc.append('### Principles of the Comprehensive Transesophageal Examination')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('Transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) is an indispensable clinical modality that overcomes the acoustic window limitations of transthoracic imaging. The physical proximity of the esophagus and stomach to the posterior aspect of the heart permits the use of high-frequency transducers ($5	ext{--}7\text{ MHz}$), yielding superior spatial and temporal resolution of intracardiac anatomy, valves, and great vessels:')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('1. **Standardized 28-View Protocol:**')
    doc.append('   - A complete comprehensive examination comprises **28 standardized cross-sectional views** acquired across four acoustic levels: **Upper Esophageal (UE)**, **Mid-Esophageal (ME)**, **Transgastric (TG)**, and **Deep Transgastric (Deep TG)**.')
    doc.append('   - Each standard view requires multiplane angle rotation ($0^\circ	ext{--}180^\circ$) and coordinated probe manipulation (advancement, withdrawal, right/left rotation, anteflexion, retroflexion, right/left lateral flexion).')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('2. **Integration of 3D Echocardiography:**')
    doc.append('   - Real-time 3D matrix-array imaging (live narrow-angle, live wide-angle zoom, full-volume multi-beat, and 3D color Doppler) is integrated into the routine protocol.')
    doc.append('   - 3D imaging is the diagnostic standard for mitral valve prolapse mapping, aortic annulus non-planar geometry, tricuspid valve morphology, and complex atrial septal defect sizing.')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('3. **Patient Safety, Sedation, and Contraindications:**')
    doc.append('   - TEE is an semi-invasive procedure requiring rigorous pre-procedure screening for esophageal pathology, strict adherence to ASA physical status classification, standardized conscious sedation protocols, and post-procedure recovery monitoring (Modified Aldrete Score $\ge 9$ for discharge).')
    doc.append('   - Absolute contraindications (perforated viscus, active upper GI bleeding, esophageal stricture/tumor) and relative contraindications (varices, Barrett\'s esophagus, severe cervical spine disease) must be systematically excluded.')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('</div></details>')
