    # Section 4: Three-Dimensional TEE Protocol
    doc.append('<details class="med-details"><summary>')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('## 4. Three-Dimensional (3D) TEE Examination Protocol</summary><div class="details-content">')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('### 3D Acquisition Modalities')
    doc.append('Real-time 3D matrix-array probes provide four core acquisition modes:')
    doc.append('1. **Live 3D (Narrow-Angle):** Real-time pyramidal volume (up to $30^\circ \times 60^\circ$) rendered instantaneously at high temporal resolution without ECG gating. Ideal for dynamic valve leaflet motion.')
    doc.append('2. **3D Zoom:** Focused high-resolution volume with user-defined region of interest (ROI) cropped tightly around a target structure (mitral valve, aortic valve, LAA).')
    doc.append('3. **Full-Volume (Wide-Angle):** Stitched multi-beat volume ($2	ext{--}7\text{ beats}$) providing wide field of view ($90^\circ \times 90^\circ$). Requires stable rhythm and breath-hold to prevent stitch artifacts.')
    doc.append('4. **3D Color Flow Doppler:** Superimposes color Doppler velocity maps within a 3D pyramid, essential for mapping eccentric vena contracta area.')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('<span id="fig-05"></span>')
    doc.append('![Figure 5: 3D TEE acquisition steps: Narrow-angle mode](images/fig05_3d_acquisition_mitral_narrow_angle.jpg)')
    doc.append('*Figure 5: Three-dimensional transesophageal echocardiographic acquisition steps for narrow-angle mode. Centering the region of interest in two orthogonal 2D planes prior to activating real-time 3D rendering.*')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('<span id="fig-06"></span>')
    doc.append('![Figure 6: 3D TEE acquisition steps: Wide-angle zoom mode](images/fig06_3d_acquisition_mitral_wide_angle.jpg)')
    doc.append('*Figure 6: Three-dimensional transesophageal echocardiographic acquisition steps for wide-angle zoom mode. Optimizing spatial lateral and elevation boundaries to maximize volume rate.*')
    doc.append('')
