    doc.append('## 6. Adult Congenital Heart Disease (ACHD) TEE Imaging Algorithm</summary><div class="details-content">')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('### Table 12: Recommended TEE Imaging Views in Selected ACHD Diagnostic Scenarios')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('| Congenital Defect | Primary Diagnostic Views | Essential TEE Checklist & Measurements |')
    doc.append('| :--- | :--- | :--- |')
    doc.append('| **Secundum Atrial Septal Defect (ASD)** | ME Bicaval ($90^\circ	ext{--}110^\circ$), ME 4Ch ($0^\circ$), ME AV SAX ($30^\circ	ext{--}60^\circ$) | Measure maximal defect diameter and area; assess all six rim margins (superior, inferior, retro-aortic, posterior, AV valve, and IVC rims; rim $\ge 5\text{ mm}$ required for device closure). |')
    doc.append('| **Primum ASD / Partial AV Canal** | ME 4Ch ($0^\circ$), ME Mitral Commissural ($60^\circ$) | Interrogate low defect adjacent to AV valve rings; evaluate anterior mitral leaflet cleft; assess degree of left AV valve regurgitation. |')
    doc.append('| **Sinus Venosus ASD** | High ME Bicaval ($90^\circ	ext{--}110^\circ$) and modified bicaval | Defect at SVC-RA or IVC-RA junction; identify anomalous partial pulmonary venous drainage (e.g., RUPV entering SVC). |')
    doc.append('| **Ventricular Septal Defect (VSD)** | ME AV SAX ($30^\circ	ext{--}60^\circ$), ME 4Ch ($0^\circ$), ME LAX ($120^\circ$) | Classify type: perimembranous (adjacent to tricuspid septal leaflet and aortic NCC/RCC), muscular, inlet, or outlet/supracristal. Quantify peak shunt velocity and shunt direction. |')
    doc.append('| **Tetralogy of Fallot (Repaired)** | ME RV Inflow-Outflow ($60^\circ$), Deep TG, UE Arch | Pulmonary regurgitation severity, RVOT conduit stenosis/aneurysm, residual VSD, aortic root dilation. |')
    doc.append('| **Coarctation of the Aorta** | UE Aortic Arch LAX ($0^\circ$) and SAX ($80^\circ$) | Discrete shelf narrowing distal to left subclavian artery; continuous-wave Doppler "sawtooth" diastolic runoff. |')
    doc.append('| **Persistent Left Superior Vena Cava** | ME Bicaval ($90^\circ$) and ME 2Ch ($90^\circ$) | Markedly dilated coronary sinus ($> 10\text{ mm}$); confirm PLSVC by injecting agitated saline in left arm (bubbles fill CS before right atrium). |')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('</div></details>')
